{"name":"Deadsy","hex":"#c2a84b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Deadsy","blocks":[{"text":"Deadsy is an American rock band from Los Angeles. Formed by Elijah Blue Allman in 1995, the band is characterized by analog keyboard and guitar synthesizers, Allman's baritone vocals, theatrical image and retro 1980s gothic rock style. Their fanbase is referred to as the Legion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c5/Deadsy_promotional_2002.jpg/330px-Deadsy_promotional_2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deadsy","wikidata":"Q1180956"},{"title":"Deadsy (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Deadsy is the debut studio album by American rock band Deadsy. It was scheduled for release on February 25, 1997, by Sire Records. Several promotional compact discs and compact cassettes of the album, as well as a CD-single for \"The Elements\", were sent out to members of the press and radio stations, but the release was pulled less than a month before its release date by distributor Elektra Entertainment Group. Sire Records eventually secured a new distribution deal through Warner Music Group but it was again shelved; the release ultimately evolved into Commencement in 1998."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/25/Deadsy_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deadsy_(album)","wikidata":"Q5245717"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Gold nugget (placer gold) 1 (17001285916)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Gold_nugget_%28placer_gold%29_1_%2817001285916%29.jpg/500px-Gold_nugget_%28placer_gold%29_1_%2817001285916%29.jpg","ratio":1.266304347826087,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_nugget_(placer_gold)_1_(17001285916).jpg","share":0.118125},{"title":"Multiple rows of golden statues of the Bu